# 4-bit MLX weights. The everyday model; Shift+Tab adds thinking, and pi
# sends sampling to match the level, so this file's values are the fallback
# for `ollama run` outside pi.
# Sampling values are Qwen's published instruct-mode settings. Wrong sampling
# hurts these models more than quantisation does.
FROM qwen3.8:27b-mlx
# 65536. An earlier revision cut this to 40960 believing the prefix-cache
# evictions were a capacity problem. That was wrong. Ollama ran with
# OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL:1, so it held a single cache slot, and two agent sessions
# taking turns through one slot evict each other on every turn. The log shows it
# plainly: requests alternating between a small conversation and a large one,
# each restoring only part of its matched prefix. Lowering the window changed
# nothing, because the window was never the constraint: eight evictions still
# happened in thirty minutes with sixteen gigabytes of headroom spare.
#
# The fix is slots, not size. With OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL at 2 each concurrent
# conversation keeps its own cache, so the window goes back to 65536.
#
# The cost is memory, and it is not small: KV is roughly 111 KB per token, so
# two slots at this window is about 14.5 GB of cache on top of 18.5 GB of
# weights. Watch /doctor. If evictions return with only one session running,
# that is a real capacity limit and this number should come down again.
PARAMETER num_ctx 65536
PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER presence_penalty 1.5
